HTML Crash Course
The HTML file has 3 fixed parts that never change and 1 part that changes every exam.

The Fixed Parts (copy blindly every exam)
1 — The head (always identical)
html<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/icon?family=Material+Icons" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/materialize/1.0.0/css/materialize.min.css">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
    <title>LE App</title>
    <style>
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body { display: flex; height: 100vh; flex-direction: column; overflow: hidden; }
      main { flex: 1; display: flex; width: 100%; overflow: hidden; }
      .panel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; overflow: hidden; border-right: 1px solid #ddd; }
      .scroll-area { overflow-y: auto; flex: 1; padding: 6px 10px; }
      .card { margin: 4px 0; }
    </style>
  </head>
2 — The nav (only change the app name)
html  <nav class="purple">
    <div class="nav-wrapper" style="padding: 0 12px;">
      <span class="brand-logo left" style="font-size:1.1em; line-height:56px;">
        LE App — {{ current_user.username }}
        <!--        ↑ only change "LE App" to the exam app name -->
      </span>
      <ul class="right">
        <li><a href="/logout">Logout</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </nav>
3 — Flash messages (never change)
html  {% with messages = get_flashed_messages(request) %}
    {% if messages %}
      <div style="padding: 4px 12px;">
        {% for message in messages %}
          <div class="card-panel blue lighten-5" style="margin:2px 0; padding:6px 12px;">
            {{ message }}
          </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  {% endwith %}
4 — Scripts at the bottom (never change)
html  <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/materialize/1.0.0/js/materialize.min.js"></script>
  <script>M.AutoInit();</script>
</body>
</html>

The Part That Changes — Inside <main>
This is where you build your panels. The exam figure tells you how many columns there are. Each column = one div with the class panel.

The 5 Building Blocks
These are the only things you ever build inside <main>. Mix and match depending on the exam.

Block 1 — Loop over a list of items (left panel)
html<div class="panel" style="width: 30%;">
  <h6 style="padding:8px 12px; margin:0; font-weight:bold;">Albums</h6>
  <!--                                                         ↑ change heading -->
  <div class="scroll-area">
    {% for album in albums %}
    <!--        ↑ change to your variable name -->
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-content">
          <p><strong>{{ album.title }}</strong></p>
          <!--              ↑ your field name -->
          <p class="grey-text">{{ album.artist }}</p>
          <!--                      ↑ second field or remove -->
          <a href="/album/{{ album.id }}" class="btn-small purple waves-effect">View</a>
          <!--           ↑ your route    ↑ your id -->
        </div>
      </div>
    {% else %}
      <p style="color:grey; padding:10px;">Nothing here yet.</p>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>

Block 2 — Show children of selected parent (middle panel)
html<div class="panel" style="width: 38%;">
  <h6 style="padding:8px 12px; margin:0; font-weight:bold;">
    {% if active_album %}{{ active_album.title }}{% else %}Select an album{% endif %}
    <!--       ↑ your active variable                    ↑ your field     -->
  </h6>
  <div class="scroll-area">
    {% if active_album %}
      {% for track in active_album.tracks %}
      <!--   ↑ child var   ↑ parent     ↑ relationship field name -->
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-content" style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center;">
            <span>{{ track.title }}</span>
            <!--        ↑ child field -->
            <a href="/track/{{ track.id }}" class="btn-small purple waves-effect">View</a>
            <!--            ↑ your route -->
          </div>
        </div>
      {% else %}
        <p style="color:grey;">No tracks yet.</p>
      {% endfor %}
    {% else %}
      <p style="color:grey; padding:10px;">Select something from the left.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>

Block 3 — Add item form
html<form method="POST" action="/track/{{ active_track.id }}/comment">
<!--                         ↑ your POST route -->
  <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; align-items:center; padding:8px 10px;">
    <div class="input-field" style="flex:1; margin:0;">
      <input type="text" id="comment_text" name="text" required>
      <!--                                       ↑ must match Form() param in route -->
      <label for="comment_text">Write a comment...</label>
      <!--                                      ↑ change placeholder -->
    </div>
    <button class="btn purple waves-effect" type="submit">Add</button>
  </div>
</form>

Block 4 — List with delete button (right panel)
html<div class="scroll-area">
  <ul class="collection" style="margin:0; border:none;">
    {% for comment in active_track.comments %}
    <!--   ↑ your var   ↑ active item  ↑ relationship field -->
      <li class="collection-item" style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center;">
        <div>
          <strong>{{ comment.user.username }}:</strong> {{ comment.text }}
          <!--                ↑ who wrote it                    ↑ content field -->
        </div>
        {% if comment.user_id == current_user.id %}
        <!--          ↑ only show delete to the owner -->
          <a href="/comment/{{ comment.id }}/delete" class="red-text">
            <i class="material-icons">delete</i>
          </a>
        {% endif %}
      </li>
    {% else %}
      <li class="collection-item grey-text">Nothing here yet.</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</div>

Block 5 — Like/dislike buttons
html<form method="POST" action="/track/{{ active_track.id }}/react">
<!--                                ↑ your react route -->
  <div style="padding:6px 10px;">
    <button type="submit" name="action" value="like" class="btn-small green waves-effect">
    <!--                        ↑ must match Form() param   ↑ must match if check in route -->
      <i class="material-icons left">thumb_up</i>{{ active_track.likes }}
      <!--                                                  ↑ your likes field -->
    </button>
    <button type="submit" name="action" value="dislike" class="btn-small red waves-effect" style="margin-left:6px;">
      <i class="material-icons left">thumb_down</i>{{ active_track.dislikes }}
    </button>
  </div>
</form>

The Rules to Remember
Jinja2 syntax:
{{ variable }}           → print a value
{% if something %}       → condition (always needs {% endif %})
{% for x in list %}      → loop (always needs {% endfor %})
{% else %}               → works inside both if and for
Dot notation vs dict:
{{ album.title }}        → use dot for DB model objects
{{ item["name"] }}       → use square brackets for API dicts
Forms:
method="GET"   → search forms and filter forms
method="POST"  → add, react, award — anything that changes data
The name= rule:
html<input name="text">   ← this must match exactly →   text: str = Form(...)
<input name="rating"> ← this must match exactly →   rating: int = Form(...)

How to Read the Figure in the Exam

Count the columns → that's how many panels you need
Left column = Block 1 always
Middle column = Block 2 if there's a parent/child
Right column = Block 3 + Block 4 for forms and lists
If there are like/dislike buttons → add Block 5 at the top of the right panel

